findings.message:
[LLM] Missing card ownership validation. User could freeze cards they don't own by passing any card_id in kwargs. | Suggestion: Add validation: `card_id = kwargs.get('card_id')
if not card_id: raise ValueError('card_id is required')
if not self.auth_service.user_owns_card(user_id, card_id): raise PermissionError('User does not own this card')`

[LLM] Missing idempotency check. Per acceptance criteria, freezing an already-frozen card should return HTTP 400, but code doesn't check current card status. | Suggestion: Before freezing: `current_status = self._get_card_status(card_id)
if current_status == 'FROZEN': raise ValueError('Card is already frozen')
if current_status not in ['ACTIVE', 'UNFROZEN']: raise ValueError(f'Cannot freeze card in {current_status} status')`

[LLM] Missing card state validation. Acceptance criteria requires HTTP 400 for already-active or non-existent cards, but there's no check of current card state before unfreezing. | Suggestion: Before unfreezing: card_state = get_card_state(kwargs['card_id'])
if not card_state: raise ValueError('Card not found')
if card_state == 'ACTIVE': raise ValueError('Card is already active')
if card_state != 'FROZEN': raise ValueError('Card cannot be unfrozen from current state')
